T:Hello, Echo
C:Grand Central Stationery (AI-assisted original, CC0)
O:Course original (no cultural attribution)
R:JK greeting and echo song
S:Grand Central Stationery, Ontario Listening Bridges (original course composition, 11 November 2026), CC0 1.0
N:Original JK greeting and echo song; a leader sings a two-bar greeting and the class echoes it at once, choosing loud or soft for the first echo and singing or clapping the rhythm for the second.
N:Listen: Ella Jenkins — "You'll Sing a Song and I'll Sing a Song", title track of the album You'll Sing a Song and I'll Sing a Song, with members of the Urban Gateways Children's Chorus (Folkways FC 7664, 1966; Smithsonian Folkways SFW 45010 reissue), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u60cDWfAMBo. Notice how a leader leaves room for a real answer; compare an exact echo with an answer that changes one thing, such as how loud it is.
N:Ella Jenkins (1924-2024), a Chicago-based singer and educator, made call-and-response with children central to her recordings; this 1966 album was added to the Library of Congress National Recording Registry in 2007. This tiny original greeting is a listening doorway, not a transcription of her melody or words.
N:Original melody, words and form; the named recording is for listening and discussion only and is linked from the Smithsonian Folkways auto-generated channel, not embedded. Do not label this as an Ella Jenkins song.
N:Published early: an AI-assisted original written for this course and released CC0, not traditional and not by any artist named above. Not yet tried with a class or read by its reviewers (Early-years (JK) music teacher, JK classroom trial and a second score reader); its workshop record is kept for correction.
