T:Gong Garden
T:Original Grade 2 AB song for little bells and a big gong
C:Grand Central Stationery (AI-assisted original, CC0)
O:Course original (no cultural attribution)
R:Grade 2 AB song with bordun
S:Grand Central Stationery, Ontario Listening Bridges (original course composition, 11 November 2026), CC0 1.0
N:Original Grade 2 AB song contrasting short and long sounds: a quick "little bells" A section and a slow "big gong" B section over a do-so bordun, with bell and gong players as layers.
N:Listen: Gamelan Sekar Jaya — "Legong Lasem" (performance video, Gamelan Sekar Jaya official YouTube channel, 30 January 2021; music director I Dewa Putu Berata, dance director Shoko Yamamuro), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=irmtW9E4Y6Y. Listen for nested time: quick interlocking tones inside slower punctuation from larger gongs.
N:Gamelan names many distinct ensemble traditions of Indonesia, above all in Bali and Java. Gamelan Sekar Jaya is a Balinese gamelan and dance company in Berkeley, California, co-founded in 1979 with the Balinese musician I Wayan Suweca and long taught by visiting Balinese artists. Legong is one of Bali's classical dances, accompanied by a gamelan in which fast interlocking parts move inside a slow cycle marked by gongs. This original pentatonic classroom piece compares quick and slow layers; it is not a gamelan composition and must not be labelled Balinese music.
N:Original notes, words and form; no named composition, tuning, kotekan (interlocking) pattern, melody or gong cycle is copied. The classroom pentatonic is the Western do-re-mi-so-la scale, not a Balinese pelog or slendro tuning.
N:Published early: an AI-assisted original written for this course and released CC0, not traditional and not by any artist named above. Not yet tried with a class or read by its reviewers (Grade 2 classroom music teacher, Indonesian (Balinese) gamelan educator, second score reader); its workshop record is kept for correction.
