N:Original Grade 2 verse-and-chorus song over a do-so bordun, in which the second verse varies the first and a soloist adds a variation of their own.
N:Listen: Toumani Diabaté — "Jarabi", from the solo kora album Kaira (Hannibal Records, 1988; recorded in London, October 1987), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=asvPlOGh5tI. Hear how a repeating foundation supports delicate variation and a long melodic line.
N:Toumani Diabaté (1965-2024), from Bamako, Mali, was born into a family of jeli (griots), the hereditary musicians and keepers of history of the Mande world, and played the 21-string kora, a harp-lute from that tradition. Kaira (1988) was the first album of solo kora; on it a repeating accompaniment figure and running variations share one instrument. This new pentatonic song for voices and barred instruments is not a kora piece.
N:Original tune, words and bordun; no kora figure, "Jarabi" melody or lyric is transcribed, and the bordun is a classroom do-so drone, not a kumbengo (kora accompaniment pattern).
