N:Original Grade 4 song and listening bridge for syncopation and major/minor contrast; the class sings a lantern phrase in C major, then the same notes in C minor, before listening for son's repeating cycle and its singer-and-chorus conversation in "Chan Chan".
N:Listen: Buena Vista Social Club — "Chan Chan" (Compay Segundo), opening track of the album "Buena Vista Social Club" (World Circuit, June 1997), recorded at EGREM, Havana, in March 1996, https://www.buenavistasocialclub.com/albums/buena-vista-social-club/. Track the repeating harmonic cycle, the conversational vocal delivery and the independent percussion timeline.
N:The recording can introduce Cuban son, Compay Segundo (Francisco Repilado, 1907-2003), who wrote "Chan Chan", and the late-twentieth-century international attention to veteran Cuban musicians around the Buena Vista Social Club album. This new syncopation study is not son and uses no "Chan Chan" material.
N:Original melody, lyric, rhythm and harmony; no tres figure, bass line, clave pattern or the song's four-chord minor cycle is copied. The classroom harmony is a plain C-Am-F-C cycle answered by Cm-Ab-Fm-G-Cm.
