N:Original 12-bar teaching blues for Grade 7; the class plays the written call in each line, a soloist answers in the two bars of rest that follow, and everyone plays the closing line together.
N:Listen: Little Walter — "Juke" (Checker, 1952), a 12-bar Chicago blues for harmonica, recorded with Muddy Waters's band, https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HxkqDe7DN8g. Hear the 12-bar form go round, the harmonica's riffs and the band's answers.
N:Little Walter (Marion Walter Jacobs) recorded "Juke" in Chicago in 1952 with musicians from Muddy Waters's band; Chicago blues joined the Mississippi Delta's blues, the electric guitar and amplified harmonica, and the Great Migration of Black Southerners to northern cities.
N:Original riff, melody and answer windows, with no words; nothing from "Juke" is used.
