N:Original two-part interlock and layered-form study for Grade 8 on classroom barred instruments (or recorders, keyboards, bells): two groups learn to make one line together without colliding, then shape the form by adding, swapping and thinning layers, alongside listening to a Balinese gamelan composition by I Nyoman Windha.
N:Listen: I Nyoman Windha — "Puspanjali" (1989), music for the welcome dance of the same name, played by STSI Denpasar (Aneka Record), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=R8_NjuIhGn8. Hear coordinated interlocking parts, sectional contrast, paired tuning shimmer and large-scale punctuation.
N:Balinese gamelan composition is a living, changing art with ensemble-specific tuning and rehearsal practice. This equal-tempered classroom polyphony is not gamelan and does not reproduce kotekan.
N:Original notes and sectional plan; no Windha passage, tuning, interlocking pattern or gong structure is copied.
